3. Features and Functionalities Implemented

🔐 Secure Authentication
User Sign Up/Login using Clerk
Role-based access control
Session management

🏢 Workspace & Organization Management
Create and manage multiple organizations/workspaces
Workspace-specific team collaboration

📁 Project Management
Create new projects
Edit/Delete projects
Track project progress
Set priorities and deadlines

✅ Task Management
Create and assign tasks
Update task status
Track deadlines
Task lifecycle management

👥 Team Collaboration
Invite team members via email
Assign roles
Collaborate within workspace

🔔 Automated Notifications
Background notification processing using Inngest
Deadline reminders
Task assignment alerts

📊 Dashboard & Analytics
Project statistics
Task overview
Progress monitoring
Overdue task tracking
🗄 Database Management
Relational database schema
Project, User, Workspace, and Task tables
Prisma ORM integration

☁ Cloud Deployment
Frontend deployment using Vercel
Cloud-hosted PostgreSQL database using Neon

Features are described throughout the report including functional requirements and modules.

4. Installation / Execution Steps to Run the Project
Prerequisites

Install the following software:

Node.js (v18 or above)
PostgreSQL
Git

Step 1: Clone Repository
git clone https://github.com/avirajj93-commits/Project-Management.git

Step 2: Setup Frontend
cd client
npm install
npm run dev

Step 3: Setup Backend
cd server
npm install

Step 4: Configure Environment Variables

Create .env files inside both client and server folders and add:

DATABASE_URL=
CLERK_SECRET_KEY=
VITE_CLERK_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=
INNGEST_EVENT_KEY=

Step 5: Run Database Migration
npx prisma db push

Step 6: Start Backend Server
npm start

Step 7: Open Application

Frontend:

http://localhost:5173

Backend:

http://localhost:3000

Installation instructions are also included in the project report.

